{
  "capture": "telemetry/mg90-b__dev-v006-2A-D",
  "notes": "identification reads stage 2's mg90-b captures as a servo's board alone could and grades each route against stage 2's bench references; it scores no speed. Each route key is a quantity, value and bounds, with reference, error_pct (or error_ma), spread and cost beside it. r_one_seat_ohm, r_two_seats_ohm, r_three_seats_ohm: rest-resistance's stall pass, a seat's R the mean of its two graded 100 % laps (3.7 and 4.2 V, direction +1, the line through V/I back to the lap's start), every combination of k of the 12 holes; value the median, bounds the lowest and highest; reference the 12-hole mean; error_pct sd over the combinations with the extremes as bounds; error_angle_part_pct the same with rest-resistance's one-body heat taken out; spread_pct the laps' own scatter about a hole's mean. r_board_ntc_move_pct: copper's 0.39 %/C times the board NTC (nominal beta, at each folder's rest baseline) less T_ref, the board at the stall pass's graded laps, over capture-1, speed-torque and swapped-1's folders; self_heat_bound_pct the winding's rise bounded by rest-resistance's warming_pct_per_j for a spin's own joules and its one-body map (0.716 %/J held, tau 90 s) for heat carried. r_reference_rung: capture-1's 5 V 15 % running R at the cut, (V_mean - E0)/i_hat, the per-spin sd with direction means out, the spins per check for 0.5 % on a change, and the trend over the sitting. ke_v_s_per_rad: one repeat's 20 coasts (e_win over the ripple count), the three repeats as the value and bounds; error_pct held out on the other two repeats. l_mh, l_ripple_mh: inductance's capture-1 bursts at one seat, 4 bursts at 25 % forward with the group's first thrown out, the 12 holes as value and bounds; error_pct against the 12-hole median of the same design. c_a_s_per_v: c = i100 / (Ke (alpha_drive + alpha_coast)) from one speed-torque run-up per direction, the three passes, by the coast's 5 ms windows and its pinned read. delta_f_ma_per_v: the reading term per volt by the 100 % anchor, crest less anchor over 50 ms windows of one capture-1 repeat with that pass's c, the three passes; error_ma the mean over capture-1's rungs at their own v_on against the published no-meter grid. v_b_mv: the speed table by mechanical direction from one repeat of 7.4 V 30/40/60 % both ways, 50 ms windows, reference R, Ke and Delta; value the median over the three passes, bounds the range; reference the full-data table (all repeats, 200 ms). X = V_mean - Ke w_tach - R i_hat is split as a speed table plus k_d_mv_per_dropout_s times the dropout rate (rows of the window under dropout_threshold of its mean, per second); the table is the speed part; floor_mv is the table at and below 150 rev/s, the low rungs' mean unless the rails split (floor_by_rail_mv), then 0; dropout_ambiguous_share is the share of the rows under 0.40 of the mean that sit within 0.10 to 0.40, the threshold's gap. Costs by the board's rough speed, (D v_on - R i)/Ke, a short spin the spin-up to 95 % of speed, the window and 15 ms of coast; the anchor run-up's revs by speed-torque's turn-window tach.",
